 been significantly improved yet. Let me start by checking GPU availability and running the profiler to get fresh measurements. marks\n3. Profile with nsight\n\nLet me first check the GPU, then run benchmarks.\n\nWait - I should also check the current metrics files to see if they're already up-to-date. Let me check what's in current_apc300_metrics.json.\n\nActually, let me first check whether the current measurements are up-to-date or need to be re-run. The git status shows modified files for current_apc000.json, current_apc100.json, current_apc300.json which suggests they were recently updated. Let me check the existing current metrics files and see if they match the latest state of the code.\n\nActually, let me just proceed methodically. Let me:\n1. Check GPU is free\n2. Run the benchmarks for APC 0, 100, 300\n3. Profile\n\nBut first, let me understand how to run the benchmarks. I need to locate the powdr repo and figure out the right way to invoke the benchmark script.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6789,"cache_read_input_tokens":43884,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6789},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"97849a12-7ea3-4743-9ec4-4f09ecc25100","uuid":"af6469d9-fbc5-4b98-9fcb-766cf1dad4ba"}
