oeff)?;\n200\t        current_log_step += 1;\n201\t    }\n202\t\n203\t    Ok(())\n204\t}\n205\t\n206\t/// Given vector `x` in `F^n`, populates `out` with `eq_n(x, y)` for `y` on hypercube `H_n`.\n207\t///\n208\t/// Note: This function launches `n` CUDA kernels.\n209\t///\n210\t/// The multilinear equality polynomial is defined as:\n211\t/// ```text\n212\t///     eq(x, z) = \\prod_{i=0}^{n-1} (x_i z_i + (1 - x_i)(1 - z_i)).\n213\t/// ```\n214\t///\n215\t/// # Safety\n216\t/// - `n` is set to the length of `xs`.\n217\t/// - `out` must have length `>= 2^n`.\n218\tpub unsafe fn evals_eq_hypercube(out: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>, xs: &[EF]) -> Result<(), KernelError> {\n219\t    let n = xs.len();\n220\t    assert!(out.len() >= 1 << n);\n221\t    // Use memcpy instead of memset since EF will be in Montgomery form.\n222\t    [EF::ONE].copy_to(out).map_err(KernelError::MemCopy)?;\n223\t\n224\t    for (i, &x_i) in xs.iter().enumerate() {\n225\t        let step = 1 << i;\n226\t        eq_hypercube_stage_ext(out.as_mut_ptr(), x_i, step).map_err(KernelError::Kernel)?;\n227\t    }\n228\t    Ok(())\n229\t}\n230\t\n231\t/// Given vector `u_tilde` in `F^n`, populates `out` with `mobius_eq(u_tilde, y)` for `y` on\n232\t/// hypercube `H_n`.\n233\t///\n234\t/// The Möbius-adjusted equality kernel is defined as:\n235\t/// ```text\n236\t///     mobius_eq(u_tilde, y) = \\prod_{i=0}^{n-1} ((1 - 2*u_tilde_i)(1 - y_i) + u_tilde_i * y_i).\n237\t/// ```\n238\t///\n239\t/// Note: This function launches `n` CUDA kernels.\n240\t///\n241\t/// # Safety\n242\t/// - `n` is set to the length of `omega`.\n243\t/// - `out` must have length `>= 2^n`.\n244\tpub unsafe fn evals_mobius_eq_hypercube(\n245\t    out: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n246\t    omega: &[EF],\n247\t) -> Result<(), KernelError> {\n248\t    let n = omega.len();\n249\t    assert!(out.len() >= 1 << n);"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01QfPKRE6nJ51RbYHqHWreQe","session_id":"97849a12-7ea3-4743-9ec4-4f09ecc25100","uuid":"cbb6d8d0-c1c5-408c-8dd9-70925