ifies soundness\n\n2. **Algebraic Batching** (lines 99-137):\n   - Sample randomness `mu` via Fiat-Shamir (line 96)\n   - Compute `mu.powers()` for total stacked width (line 120)\n   - **GPU Kernel Call**: `whir_algebraic_batch_traces()` (line 128)\n     - CUDA kernel: `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/whir.cu:24-74`\n     - Batches all unstacked traces into single `f_ple_evals` buffer\n     - Output: `DeviceBuffer<F>` of length `height * D_EF`\n\n3. **FFT/DFT Operations** (lines 143-166):\n   - **GPU Kernel**: `batch_ntt_small()` (line 145)\n     - iDFT per chunk of size `2^l_skip`\n     - Converts PLE evals to univariate coefficients `c_z(x)`\n   - **GPU Kernel**: `transpose_fp_to_fpext_vec()` (line 151)\n     - Converts base field buffer to extension field\n   - **GPU Kernel**: `mle_interpolate_stage_ext()` loop (lines 163-165)\n     - Applies subset-zeta transform (l_skip stages)\n     - Computes MLE coefficient form of `\\hat{f}`\n\n4. **Initial Moments Setup** (lines 175-178):\n   - **GPU Kernel**: `evals_eq_hypercube()` (line 177)\n     - Computes moment vector `w_moments` for initial equality polynomial\n\n---\n\n#### Phase 2: WHIR Sumcheck Rounds (Lines 199-271)\n\n**Loop Structure**: `for (whir_round, ...) -> for (round in 0..k_whir)`\n- **Number of iterations**: `k_whir` sumcheck rounds per WHIR round\n- **Total rounds**: `num_whir_rounds = (m - log_final_poly_len) / k_whir`\n- m = log2(stacked_height), typically m ≈ 20-24 at APC 300\n\n**Per Sumcheck Round** (lines 204-270):\n\n1. **Sumcheck Polynomial Evaluation** (lines 224-236):\n   - **GPU Kernel**: `whir_sumcheck_coeff_moments_round()` (line 224)\n     - CUDA kernel: `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/whir.cu:83-136`\n     - Computes `s(X) = sum_y f(X,y) * w(X,y)` for X ∈ {1,2}\n     - Uses pairwise formula: `f(X,y) = c0 + X*c1`, `w(X,y) = m0 + X*(m1-m0)`\n     - Block reduction + final reduce to get 2 output values\n     - Output copied to host (line 237):