und Merkle Operations** (lines 375-442):\n   - **Only in whir_round == 0** (line 375)\n   - **Batch Merkle Proof Query** (lines 399-404):\n     - **Method**: `MerkleTreeGpu::batch_query_merkle_proofs()` (line 400)\n     - `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/merkle_tree.rs:278-349`\n     - CUDA kernel: `query_digest_layers()` (line 329)\n       - Gathers merkle proof siblings from digest layers\n       - Batches across multiple trees and queries\n   - **Batch Row Openings** (lines 419-436):\n     - **Method**: `MerkleTreeGpu::batch_open_rows()` (line 419)\n     - `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/merkle_tree.rs:174-230`\n     - CUDA kernel: `matrix_get_rows_fp_kernel()` (line 211)\n       - Reads rows from backing matrix in strided pattern\n       - Per-tree but iterated (lines 202-228)\n       - D2H copy: `d_out.to_host()` (line 222)\n   - **Memory Cleanup** (line 442):\n     - Drops `stacked_per_commit` to free RS codeword matrices\n\n6. **Subsequent Round Merkle Queries** (lines 444-464):\n   - Re-use `rs_tree` from previous round\n   - Same batch proof/row opening pattern\n\n7. **Update Weight Moments** (lines 470-511):\n   - **Only if not last round** (line 472)\n   - Prepare power vectors on host (lines 482-496)\n   - Copy to device (lines 498-499)\n   - **GPU Kernel**: `w_moments_accumulate()` (line 501)\n     - CUDA kernel: `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/whir.cu:196-221`\n     - Updates moments: `M(T) += gamma * z0^T + sum_i gamma^{i+1} * z_i^T`\n\n---\n\n### CUDA Kernels & Line Numbers\n\n| Kernel | File | Lines | Purpose | Time Impact |\n|--------|------|-------|---------|-------------|\n| `whir_algebraic_batch_traces_kernel` | whir.cu | 24-74 | Algebraically batch traces with mu powers | Setup phase |\n| `whir_sumcheck_coeff_moments_round_kernel` | whir.cu | 83-136 | Compute sumcheck polynomial evaluations | **Per-round bottleneck** |\n| `whir_fold_coeffs_and_moments_kernel` | whir.cu | 141-166 | Fold both f and w for next round | Per-round |\n| `w_moments_accumulate_kernel` | whir.cu | 196-221 | Add query contributions to moments | Between rounds |\n\n**CUDA FFI Wrappers**: `/home/georg/stark-backend/src/cuda/whir.rs:56-160`\n\n---\n\n### Merkle Tree Operations (Time-Critical)\n\n**Key Methods**:\n\n1. **`MerkleTreeGpu::new_generic_with_hash()`** (merkle_tree.rs:113-172):\n   - Compress rows → leaf hashes\n   - Layer-by-layer tree construction\n   - **Time**: ~O(N log N) hashes where N = codeword domain size\n\n2. **`batch_query_merkle_proofs()`** (merkle_tree.rs:278-349):\n   - CUDA kernel `query_digest_layers()` batches digest gathering\n   - D2H copy of proof siblings\n   - **Time**: ~O(depth * num_queries * num_trees)\n\n3. **`batch_open_rows()`** (merkle_tree.rs:174-230):\n   - CUDA kernel `matrix_get_rows_fp_kernel()` for each tree\n   - D2H copy of opened rows\n   - **Time**: ~O(num_queries * rows_per_query * width)\n\n---\n\n### Where the 125ms is Spent (APC 300 estimate)\n\nBased on code structure at APC 300:\n- **m ≈ 20-21** (log stacked height)\n- **k_whir = 2** (typical)\n- **num_whir_rounds = 9-10**\n- **num_queries ≈ 8-16** per round\n\n**Breakdown** (~125ms total):\n\n1. **Algebraic batching + FFTs** (lines 99-166): ~10-15ms\n   - `whir_algebraic_batch_traces`: ~5ms (single pass)\n   - `batch_ntt_small + mle_interpolate`: ~5-10ms\n\n2. **Sumcheck rounds** (lines 199-271): ~40-50ms\n   - Per round: 2 GPU kernels (sumcheck + fold)\n   - 9-10 rounds × ~5ms = ~45-50ms\n\n3. **Merkle tree construction** (per round): ~20-30ms total across all rounds\n   - Initial round tree: ~5-10ms (largest codeword)\n   - Subsequent trees: ~2-5ms each (halved size)\n   - Tree layers: log(domain) = 9-10 hash compressions\n\n4. **Merkle proof queries** (per round): ~20-25ms total\n   - Batch query kernels: ~10-15ms\n   - D2H copies: ~5-10ms (proof + row data)\n\n5. **Proof-of-work grinding**: ~10-20ms\n   - `transcript.grind_gpu()` calls between rounds\n\n---\n\n### W