{"type":"system","subtype":"task_started","task_id":"a3353bbc12b945b3f","tool_use_id":"toolu_01FzJCGfuL1RSheRVC5YTeLs","description":"Review optimization plan","task_type":"local_agent","prompt":"You are reviewing an implementation plan for a GPU prover optimization. Read these files and then review the plan according to the review guideline.\n\nRead the following files in order:\n1. `/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt/review_guideline.md` — the review standard to follow\n2. `/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt/context.md` — project context\n3. `/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md` — the task being planned\n4. `/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-16-1600-adaptive-merkle-hash-block-size/plan.md` — the plan to review\n\nThen verify the plan against the actual code:\n- Read `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/merkle_tree.cu` to verify the kernel and launcher code match what the plan describes\n- Read `crates/cuda-common/include/launcher.cuh` to verify the `kernel_launch_params` function\n- Read `crates/cuda-backend/src/merkle_tree.rs` to verify the Rust-side callers\n- Read `crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_pcs.rs` (lines 48-84) to verify the stacked_commit function\n\nReview the plan following the review guideline. Check:\n1. Does the plan correctly describe the current code?\n2. Is the adaptive blockDim.x logic correct and safe?\n3. Is the shared memory calculation correct after reducing blockDim.x?\n4. Is the expected performance improvement realistic based on the compute analysis?\n5. Are there any edge cases or failure modes not addressed?\n6. Is the plan specific enough to implement without inventing missing design?\n\nReturn your response in the format: Findings, Improvements, Assessment.","uuid":"e89dfaae-1e00-4a0f-aea5-d72059559f1b","session_id":"97849a12-7ea3-4743-9ec4-4f09ecc25100"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You are reviewing an implementation plan for a GPU prover optimization. Read these files and then review the plan according to the review guideline.\n\nRead the following files in order:\n1. `/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt/review_guideline.md` — the review standard to follow\n2. `/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt/context.md` — project context\n3. `/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md` — the task being planned\n4. `/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-16-1600-adaptive-merkle-hash-block-size/plan.md` — the plan to review\n\nThen verify the plan against the actual code:\n- Read `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/merkle_tree.cu` to verify the kernel and launcher code match what the plan describes\n- Read `crates/cuda-common/include/launcher.cuh` to verify the `kernel_launch_params` function\n- Read `crates/cuda-backend/src/merkle_tree.rs` to verify the Rust-side callers\n- Read `crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_pcs.rs` (lines 48-84) to verify the stacked_commit function\n\nReview the plan following the review guideline. Check:\n1. Does the plan correctly describe the current code?\n2. Is the adaptive blockDim.x logic correct and safe?\n3. Is the shared memory calculation correct after reducing blockDim.x?\n4. Is the expected performance improvement realistic based on the compute analysis?\n5. Are there any edge cases or failure modes not addressed?\n6. Is the plan specific enough to implement without inventing missing design?\n\nReturn your response in the format: Findings, Improvements, Assessment."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01FzJCGfuL1RSheRVC5YTeLs","session_id":"97849a12-7ea3-4743-9ec4-4f09ecc25100","uuid":"7e143e34-fc3b-4d5e-9795-10856e947ca0","timestamp":"2026-04-16T13:52:44.577Z"}
