{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Untxhc5PqP45xaTbzEpgKN","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-16-1600-adaptive-merkle-hash-block-size\n2\t\n3\tIncrease GPU SM utilization for the `poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes_kernel` by adaptively reducing `blockDim.x` when `query_stride` is small. At APC 300, the trace commit merkle tree hash launches only 32 blocks (25% of 128 SMs) because `query_stride=1024` with the fixed `blockDim.x=32` gives `ceil(1024/32)=32` blocks. The kernel is overwhelmingly compute-bound (53K columns × ~6625 Poseidon2 permutations per thread vs 212MB total read at 1 TB/s), so increasing block count to 128 should yield near-linear speedup on the row hashing phase — the dominant cost in Trace Commit at APC 300.\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01FzJCGfuL1RSheRVC5YTeLs","session_id":"97849a12-7ea3-4743-9ec4-4f09ecc25100","uuid":"7f561df8-b798-4f99-8b4e-7f4765bae530","timestamp":"2026-04-16T13:52:48.493Z"}
