already small (2-4ms per segment), so the main win is just reducing launch overhead. I need to find something with bigger impact.\n\nLet me step back and think about what optimization would actually move the needle here. I should commit to a plan that's realistic, implementable, hasn't been tried yet, and has measurable expected impact.\n\nI'm settling on batching the stacked reduction Round 0 and PLE fold launches using descriptor arrays—this should save 5-10ms per segment, or 10-20ms total, which is the most realistic gain I can squeeze out at this point.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3047,"cache_read_input_tokens":230594,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3047},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"97849a12-7ea3-4743-9ec4-4f09ecc25100","uuid":"35a6d768-7b52-4856-a5e0-0f6e385bb88a"}
