{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WwrPM2kxpHHjTs8mXM33AF","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md has been updated successfully."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"97849a12-7ea3-4743-9ec4-4f09ecc25100","uuid":"5bc3ec1b-ee77-40f7-ab7c-82feba3a8ac9","timestamp":"2026-04-16T14:26:41.645Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md","content":"# 2026-04-16-1600-batch-stacked-reduction-round0-descriptors\n\nBatch the per-trace stacked reduction Round 0 kernel launches (sumcheck block sums + PLE fold) using descriptor arrays. At APC 300, the stacked reduction Round 0 loop calls `stacked_reduction_sumcheck_round0` and `stacked_reduction_fold_ple` once per backing trace matrix (~400 per segment across all commits), many of which are tiny (1-2 columns, height 2^5-2^8). Grouping same-height matrices into single batched kernel launches reduces ~800 kernel launches per segment to ~100, saving kernel launch overhead and improving SM utilization for the numerous tiny launches.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":3,"newStart":1,"newLines":3,"lines":["-# 2026-04-16-1600-adaptive-merkle-hash-block-size","+# 2026-04-16-1600-batch-stacked-reduction-round0-descriptors"," ","-Increase GPU SM utilization for the `poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes_kernel` by adaptively reducing `blockDim.x` when `query_stride` is small. At APC 300, the trace commit merkle tree hash launches only 32 blocks (25% of 128 SMs) because `query_stride=1024` with the fixed `blockDim.x=32` gives `ceil(1024/32)=32` blocks. The kernel is overwhelmingly compute-bound (53K columns × ~6625 Poseidon2 permutations per thread vs 212MB total read at 1 TB/s), so increasing block count to 128 should yield near-linear speedup on the row hashing phase — the dominant cost in Trace Commit at APC 300.","+Batch the per-trace stacked reduction Round 0 kernel launches (sumcheck block sums + PLE fold) using descriptor arrays. At APC 300, the stacked reduction Round 0 loop calls `stacked_reduction_sumcheck_round0` and `stacked_reduction_fold_ple` once per backing trace matrix (~400 per segment across all commits), many of which are tiny (1-2 columns, height 2^5-2^8). Grouping same-height matrices into single batched kernel launches reduces ~800 kernel launches per segment to ~100, saving kernel launch overhead and improving SM utilization for the numerous tiny launches."]}],"originalFile":"# 2026-04-16-1600-adaptive-merkle-hash-block-size\n\nIncrease GPU SM utilization for the `poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes_kernel` by adaptively reducing `blockDim.x` when `query_stride` is small. At APC 300, the trace commit merkle tree hash launches only 32 blocks (25% of 128 SMs) because `query_stride=1024` with the fixed `blockDim.x=32` gives `ceil(1024/32)=32` blocks. The kernel is overwhelmingly compute-bound (53K columns × ~6625 Poseidon2 permutations per thread vs 212MB total read at 1 TB/s), so increasing block count to 128 should yield near-linear speedup on the row hashing phase — the dominant cost in Trace Commit at APC 300.\n"}}
