ce_width as u32, l_skip as u32) as usize;\n    if block_sums_len > self.d_block_sums.len() {\n        self.d_block_sums = DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(block_sums_len);\n    }\n\n    let lambda_pows_ptr = self.d_lambda_pows.as_ptr().add(2 * window[0]);\n    stacked_reduction_sumcheck_round0(\n        &self.eq_r_ns, trace_ptr, lambda_pows_ptr,\n        &mut self.d_block_sums, d_g_output,\n        trace_height, trace_width, l_skip,\n    );\n}\n```\n\nEach `stacked_reduction_sumcheck_round0` call launches TWO CUDA kernels:\n1. `stacked_reduction_round0_block_sum_kernel` — computes G0, G1, G2 partial block sums\n2. `final_reduce_block_sums<true>` — reduces block sums and ADDs into the G output buffer\n\n### PLE fold loop\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs`, lines 703-745\n\n```rust\nfor stacked in &self.stacked_per_commit {                // <-- per-commit loop\n    let folded_evals = DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(...);\n    folded_evals.fill_zero()?;\n    let mut dst_offset = 0;\n    for trace in &stacked.traces {                        // <-- per-trace loop\n        stacked_reduction_fold_ple(\n            trace.buffer().as_ptr(),\n            folded_evals.as_mut_ptr().add(dst_offset),\n            &self.d_omega_skip_pows, &d_inv_lagrange_denoms,\n            trace.height(), trace.width(), l_skip,\n        );\n        dst_offset += new_height * trace.width();\n    }\n    self.q_evals.push(folded_evals);                      // per-commit output\n}\n```\n\nThe fold_ple loop is nested: outer loop per commit (each commit has its own `folded_evals` buffer), inner loop per trace within that commit.\n\n### CUDA kernel signatures\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/stacked_reduction.rs`, lines 44-63\n\n```c\nfn _stacked_reduction_sumcheck_round0(\n    eq_r_ns, trace_ptr, lambda_pows, block_sums, output,\n    trace_height, trace_width, l_skip, num_x) -> i32;\n\nfn _stacked_reduction_fold_ple(\n    src, dst, omega_skip_pows, inv_lagrange_denoms,\n    trace_height, trace_width, l_skip) -> i32;\n```\n\n### nsight kernel data (APC 300, full benchmark including recursion)\n\n- `stacked_reduction_round0_block_sum_kernel`: 22ms total, 797 instances, avg 28µs\n- `final_reduce_block_sums<true>`: 7.8ms total, 797 instances, avg 10µs\n- `stacked_reduction_fold_ple_kernel`: 9ms total, 797 instances, avg 11µs\n- **Total: 38.8ms GPU, 2391 kernel launches**\n\nPer-segment wall clock:\n- Stacked reduction round 0: 14ms (seg0) + 12ms (seg1) = 26ms total\n- Of this, the GPU kernel time is ~15ms per segment (from 38.8ms / ~2.5 segments+recursion)\n- The remaining ~11ms per segment is kernel launch overhead, block_sums resize, lambda_pows pointer arithmetic\n\n### Grouping analysis\n\nTraces within a segment are grouped by height (same `n = log_height - l_skip`). At APC 300:\n- ~20 distinct heights per segment\n- Some heights have 200+ traces (e.g., APC traces with height 2^4)\n- Others have 1-5 traces (large AIRs with height 2^18+)\n\nSince `n = log_height - l_skip`, all traces of the same height map to the same G output bucket. Grouping by `trace_height` is sufficient.\n\n## Changes\n\n### Change 1: Add batched Round 0 block_sum CUDA kernel\n\n**File**: New file `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/stacked_reduction_batched.cu`\n\n```c\nstruct StackedR0Desc {\n    const Fp *trace_ptr;\n    const FpExt *lambda_pows;  // pre-offset: self.d_lambda_pows.as_ptr() + 2 * window[0]\n    uint32_t trace_width;\n    uint32_t blocks_for_this_desc;  // number of grid blocks assigned to this descriptor\n};\n\n// Maps a global blockIdx.x to a (descriptor_index, local_block_index) pair\n// using binary search on the prefix-sum of blocks_for_this_desc.\n// Follows the BlockCtx pattern from batch_mle.cu.\n```\n\nThe batched kernel reuses the existing per-trace kernel body. Each block is assigned to one descriptor via the `BlockCtx` binary search. Block sums are written to `block_sums[global_block_offset * NUM_G * skip_domain]`.\n\n**Final reduce strategy**: Call `final_reduce_block_sums<true>` per-descriptor after the batched block_sum kernel. This keeps the final reduce unchanged and simple. With ~20 height groups per segment and 1 final_reduce per descriptor within each group, the total final_reduce calls stay at ~400 per segment — but each reduce processes the blocks from just one descriptor. This is identical to the current behavior for each descriptor.\n\nRationale: The final_reduce kernel is tiny (10µs avg, 7.8ms total). Keeping it per-descriptor avoids implementing a batched reduce, adds zero risk, and the 400 launches × 5µs = 2ms overhead is acceptable relative to the savings from batching the larger block_sum kernel.\n\n### Change 2: Add batched PLE fold CUDA kernel\n\n**File**: Same file `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/stacked_reduction_batched.cu`\n\n```c\nstruct FoldPleDesc {\n    const Fp *src;        // trace buffer pointer\n    FpExt *dst;           // output buffer pointer (pre-offset within per-commit folded_evals)\n    uint32_t trace_width;\n};\n```\n\nSame BlockCtx binary search pattern. Each block processes elements from one descriptor.\n\n### Change 3: Add FFI bindings\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/stacked_reduction.rs`\n\nAdd `repr(C)` structs for `StackedR0Desc` and `FoldPleDesc`, extern \"C\" declarations for the batched launchers, and safe Rust wrapper functions.\n\n### Change 4: Orchestration in Rust — Round 0\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs`, modify `batch_sumcheck_uni_round0_poly`\n\nReplace the per-trace loop (lines 504-549) with:\n\n1. **Pre-sort by height** (already sorted via `ht_diff_idxs`): Iterate `trace_ptrs` and group consecutive traces with the same `trace_height` into batches.\n\n2. **Pre-compute max block_sums size**: `max_block_sums_len = max over all traces of _stacked_reduction_r0_required_temp_buffer_size(h, w, l_skip)`. Allocate `self.d_block_sums` once at this size.\n\n3. **For each height group** (traces with same `trace_height`):\n   a. If group has < 10 traces: process sequentially (existing code path)\n   b. If group has ≥ 10 traces:\n      - Build `Vec<StackedR0Desc>` on host. Each descriptor's `lambda_pows` field = `self.d_lambda_pows.as_ptr() + 2 * window_start_for_this_trace`. The `window_start_for_this_trace` is computed from the corresponding `ht_diff_idxs[i]`.\n      - Upload descriptor array to device: `descs.to_device()`\n      - Compute total blocks needed: sum of `blocks_for_this_desc` across all descriptors in group\n      - Allocate shared block_sums buffer for all descriptors: `total_blocks * NUM_G * skip_domain`\n      - Launch batched `block_sum` kernel with `grid = total_blocks`\n      - For each descriptor in the group: call `final_reduce_block_sums<true>` to accumulate that descriptor's block sums into the appropriate `d_g_output` buffer\n   \n   Note: All traces of the same height have the same `n`, so they all accumulate into the same G bucket (`d_g_pos` or `d_g_neg[k]`).\n\n### Change 5: Orchestration in Rust — PLE fold\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs`, modify `fold_ple_evals`\n\nBatching is scoped **within** the per-commit outer loop (lines 703-745). Within each commit:\n\n1. Group traces by `trace.height()`.\n2. For groups with ≥ 10 traces: build `FoldPleDesc` array, upload, launch batched kernel. Each descriptor's `dst` = `folded_evals.as_mut_ptr() + dst_offset_for_this_trace` (pre-computed from the sequential scan).\n3. For groups with < 10 traces: use existing per-trace path.\n\nThe per-commit `q_evals.push(folded_evals)` logic is unchanged.\n\n## Invariants\n\n1. **Correctness**: Each trace produces the same G0/G1/G2 partial block sums via the same kernel body. The block sums are reduced and added to G output identically. The fold_ple writes to the same per-trace non-overlapping output regions. Output is bit-identical to the sequential path.\n\n2. **APC 0 no-regression**: At APC 0, ~20 traces per segment. Most height groups have < 10 traces, falling below the batching threshold. The sequential path runs unchanged.\n\n3. **No VPMM pool impact**: Descriptor arrays are tiny (~400 × 24 bytes = ~10 KB). The block_sums pre-allocation replaces per-trace resizing with one upfront allocation. No per-thread accumulation buffers (the failure mode of `multistream-stacked-reduction-round0` which allocated 112 DeviceBuffers). Net memory impact is negligible.\n\n4. **fold_ple per-commit boundary**: Batching is scoped within each commit's trace loop. The per-commit `folded_evals` allocation and `q_evals.push` are unchanged.\n\n5. **lambda_pows offsets**: Each descriptor's `lambda_pows` is set to `d_lambda_pows.as_ptr() + 2 * ht_diff_idxs[i]` where `i` is the trace's index in `trace_ptrs`. This matches the current sequential computation at line 535.\n\n## Measurement Plan\n\n1. Run benchmark for APC 0, 100, 300 before and after.\n2. Compare `prover.openings.stacked_reduction.round0_time_ms` per segment.\n3. Compare `STARK (excl. trace)` overall via `spec.py`.\n4. Run nsight profile on APC 300 to verify:\n   - `stacked_reduction_round0_block_sum_kernel` instance count decreased (797 → ~80-120)\n   - `stacked_reduction_fold_ple_kernel` instance count decreased similarly\n   - `final_reduce_block_sums<true>` instance count unchanged (~797)\n   - Total kernel GPU time unchanged or slightly improved\n5. APC 0 must show no regression (within ±10ms noise on STARK excl trace).\n\n### Expected results\n\n- Launch overhead reduction: ~1400 eliminated launches × ~5µs = ~7ms across full benchmark\n- Per-segment stacked reduction round 0: 14ms → 10-12ms (seg0), 12ms → 9-11ms (seg1)\n- STARK excl trace APC 300: 1101ms → ~1087-1095ms (~6-14ms improvement)\n- APC 0: no change (below batching threshold)\n\n## Rollback Criteria\n\n- Less than 5ms improvement on stacked reduction round 0 total at APC 300.\n- Any regression > 10ms on STARK excl trace at APC 0.\n- Any correctness failure (proof verification fails at any APC configuration).\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":8,"newStart":1,"newLines":10,"lines":[" # Plan: Batch Stacked Reduction Round 0 Descriptor Arrays"," ","+*Note: Directory name is a misnomer from the first plan iteration. The actual optimization targets stacked reduction Round 0 batching, matching task.md.*","+"," ## Goal"," ","-Reduce kernel launch overhead in the stacked reduction Round 0 by batching per-trace kernel launches into per-height-group batched launches using descriptor arrays. At APC 300, the stacked reduction Round 0 calls `stacked_reduction_sumcheck_round0` and `stacked_reduction_fold_ple` once per backing trace matrix (~400 per segment across all commits), with many being tiny (1-2 columns, height 2^5-2^8). By grouping same-height traces into single batched kernel launches, we reduce ~800 kernel launches per segment to ~80, saving ~720 launches × ~5µs = ~3.6ms per segment.","+Reduce kernel launch overhead in the stacked reduction Round 0 by batching per-trace kernel launches into per-height-group batched launches using descriptor arrays. At APC 300, the stacked reduction Round 0 calls `_stacked_reduction_sumcheck_round0` (which launches 2 CUDA kernels: `stacked_reduction_round0_block_sum_kernel` + `final_reduce_block_sums<true>`) and `_stacked_reduction_fold_ple` (1 kernel) once per backing trace matrix (~400 per segment). The current total is 2391 kernel launches across both segments (797 × 3 kernel types). By batching same-height traces, we eliminate ~1400 launches."," "," ## Current Code Path"," "]},{"oldStart":15,"oldLines":14,"newStart":17,"newLines":17,"lines":["     mem::take(&mut self.trace_ptrs),","     self.ht_diff_idxs.windows(2),"," ) {","+    let log_height = trace_height.ilog2();","     let n = log_height as isize - l_skip as isize;","     let d_g_output = if n >= 0 { &mut d_g_pos } else { &mut d_g_neg[(-n-1) as usize] };"," ","-    // Per-trace temp buffer","+    let block_sums_len = _stacked_reduction_r0_required_temp_buffer_size(","+        trace_height as u32, trace_width as u32, l_skip as u32) as usize;","     if block_sums_len > self.d_block_sums.len() {","         self.d_block_sums = DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(block_sums_len);","     }"," ","+    let lambda_pows_ptr = self.d_lambda_pows.as_ptr().add(2 * window[0]);","     stacked_reduction_sumcheck_round0(","         &self.eq_r_ns, trace_ptr, lambda_pows_ptr,","         &mut self.d_block_sums, d_g_output,"]},{"oldStart":31,"oldLines":156,"newStart":36,"newLines":177,"lines":[" }"," ```"," ","-Each call launches a CUDA kernel that computes G0, G1, G2 partial sums for one trace matrix, then a final reduction kernel that ADDs block sums into the output bucket.","+Each `stacked_reduction_sumcheck_round0` call launches TWO CUDA kernels:","+1. `stacked_reduction_round0_block_sum_kernel` — computes G0, G1, G2 partial block sums","+2. `final_reduce_block_sums<true>` — reduces block sums and ADDs into the G output buffer"," "," ### PLE fold loop"," ","-**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs`, lines 714-743","+**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs`, lines 703-745"," "," ```rust","-for trace in &stacked.traces {","-    stacked_reduction_fold_ple(","-        trace.buffer().as_ptr(), dst,","-        &self.d_omega_skip_pows, &d_inv_lagrange_denoms,","-        trace.height(), trace.width(), l_skip,","-    );","-    dst_offset += new_height * trace.width();","+for stacked in &self.stacked_per_commit {                // <-- per-commit loop","+    let folded_evals = DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(...);","+    folded_evals.fill_zero()?;","+    let mut dst_offset = 0;","+    for trace in &stacked.traces {                        // <-- per-trace loop","+        stacked_reduction_fold_ple(","+            trace.buffer().as_ptr(),","+            folded_evals.as_mut_ptr().add(dst_offset),","+            &self.d_omega_skip_pows, &d_inv_lagrange_denoms,","+            trace.height(), trace.width(), l_skip,","+        );","+        dst_offset += new_height * trace.width();","+    }","+    self.q_evals.push(folded_evals);                      // per-commit output"," }"," ```"," ","-Each call launches one CUDA kernel that folds a single trace's PLE evaluations.","+The fold_ple loop is nested: outer loop per commit (each commit has its own `folded_evals` buffer), inner loop per trace within that commit."," "," ### CUDA kernel signatures"," "," **File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/stacked_reduction.rs`, lines 44-63"," "," ```c","-// Round 0: computes G0, G1, G2 block sums + final reduction","-_stacked_reduction_sumcheck_round0(","+fn _stacked_reduction_sumcheck_round0(","     eq_r_ns, trace_ptr, lambda_pows, block_sums, output,","-    trace_height, trace_width, l_skip, num_x);","+    trace_height, trace_width, l_skip, num_x) -> i32;"," ","-// PLE fold: folds trace evals by Lagrange interpolation at u_0","-_stacked_reduction_fold_ple(","+fn _stacked_reduction_fold_ple(","     src, dst, omega_skip_pows, inv_lagrange_denoms,","-    trace_height, trace_width, l_skip);","+    trace_height, trace_width, l_skip) -> i32;"," ```"," ","-### nsight kernel data (APC 300)","+### nsight kernel data (APC 300, full benchmark including recursion)"," "," - `stacked_reduction_round0_block_sum_kernel`: 22ms total, 797 instances, avg 28µs","+- `final_reduce_block_sums<true>`: 7.8ms total, 797 instances, avg 10µs"," - `stacked_reduction_fold_ple_kernel`: 9ms total, 797 instances, avg 11µs","-- Total: 31ms GPU, ~26ms wall clock (37ms + 36ms for 2 segments minus MLE portion)","-- Per-segment round 0 wall clock: 14ms (seg0), 12ms (seg1) = 26ms total","-- The ~400 launches per segment include traces from common_main + preprocessed + cached_main commits","+- **Total: 38.8ms GPU, 2391 kernel launches**"," ","-## Changes","+Per-segment wall clock:","+- Stacked reduction round 0: 14ms (seg0) + 12ms (seg1) = 26ms total","+- Of this, the GPU kernel time is ~15ms per segment (from 38.8ms / ~2.5 segments+recursion)","+- The remaining ~11ms per segment is kernel launch overhead, block_sums resize, lambda_pows pointer arithmetic"," ","-### Change 1: Add batched Round 0 CUDA kernel","+### Grouping analysis"," ","-**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/sumcheck.cu` (or a new file `stacked_reduction_batched.cu`)","+Traces within a segment are grouped by height (same `n = log_height - l_skip`). At APC 300:","+- ~20 distinct heights per segment","+- Some heights have 200+ traces (e.g., APC traces with height 2^4)","+- Others have 1-5 traces (large AIRs with height 2^18+)"," ","-Add a descriptor struct and batched kernel:","+Since `n = log_height - l_skip`, all traces of the same height map to the same G output bucket. Grouping by `trace_height` is sufficient."," ","+## Changes","+","+### Change 1: Add batched Round 0 block_sum CUDA kernel","+","+**File**: New file `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/stacked_reduction_batched.cu`","+"," ```c"," struct StackedR0Desc {","     const Fp *trace_ptr;","-    const FpExt *lambda_pows;  // already offset to this trace's position","+    const FpExt *lambda_pows;  // pre-offset: self.d_lambda_pows.as_ptr() + 2 * window[0]","     uint32_t trace_width;","+    uint32_t blocks_for_this_desc;  // number of grid blocks assigned to this descriptor"," };"," ","-// Batched kernel: processes all traces of the same height in one launch.","-// Each block processes one trace in the descriptor array.","-// Uses atomicAdd to accumulate into shared G output buffer.","-__global__ void batched_stacked_reduction_round0_kernel(","-    const FpExt *eq_r_ns,","-    const StackedR0Desc *descs,","-    const uint32_t *block_starts,  // prefix sum: which desc this block belongs to","-    uint32_t num_descs,","-    FpExt *block_sums,    // [total_blocks * NUM_G * skip_domain]","-    uint32_t trace_height, // same for all in this batch","-    uint32_t l_skip","-);","+// Maps a global blockIdx.x to a (descriptor_index, local_block_index) pair","+// using binary search on the prefix-sum of blocks_for_this_desc.","+// Follows the BlockCtx pattern from batch_mle.cu."," ```"," ","-The existing per-trace kernel body can be reused: each block computes partial G sums for its assigned trace, writing to its segment of block_sums. A final reduction kernel sums all block_sums into the G output.","+The batched kernel reuses the existing per-trace kernel body. Each block is assigned to one descriptor via the `BlockCtx` binary search. Block sums are written to `block_sums[global_block_offset * NUM_G * skip_domain]`."," ","-**Key design**: Use the `BlockCtx` binary-search pattern from the batch MLE kernel (`crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/batch_mle.cu`) to map blocks to descriptors.","+**Final reduce strategy**: Call `final_reduce_block_sums<true>` per-descriptor after the batched block_sum kernel. This keeps the final reduce unchanged and simple. With ~20 height groups per segment and 1 final_reduce per descriptor within each group, the total final_reduce calls stay at ~400 per segment — but each reduce processes the blocks from just one descriptor. This is identical to the current behavior for each descriptor."," ","+Rationale: The final_reduce kernel is tiny (10µs avg, 7.8ms total). Keeping it per-descriptor avoids implementing a batched reduce, adds zero risk, and the 400 launches × 5µs = 2ms overhead is acceptable relative to the savings from batching the larger block_sum kernel.","+"," ### Change 2: Add batched PLE fold CUDA kernel"," ","-Same approach: descriptor array with per-trace src/dst pointers.","+**File**: Same file `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/stacked_reduction_batched.cu`"," "," ```c"," struct FoldPleDesc {","-    const Fp *src;        // trace buffer","-    FpExt *dst;           // output buffer (already offset)","+    const Fp *src;        // trace buffer pointer","+    FpExt *dst;           // output buffer pointer (pre-offset within per-commit folded_evals)","     uint32_t trace_width;"," };","-","-__global__ void batched_stacked_reduction_fold_ple_kernel(","-    const FoldPleDesc *descs,","-    const uint32_t *block_starts,","-    uint32_t num_descs,","-    const Fp *omega_skip_pows,","-    const FpExt *inv_lagrange_denoms,","-    uint32_t trace_height,","-    uint32_t l_skip","-);"," ```"," ","+Same BlockCtx binary search pattern. Each block processes elements from one descriptor.","+"," ### Change 3: Add FFI bindings"," "," **File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/stacked_reduction.rs`"," ","-Add `repr(C)` structs for `StackedR0Desc` and `FoldPleDesc`, plus extern \"C\" declarations and safe wrapper functions.","+Add `repr(C)` structs for `StackedR0Desc` and `FoldPleDesc`, extern \"C\" declarations for the batched launchers, and safe Rust wrapper functions."," ","-### Change 4: Orchestration in Rust","+### Change 4: Orchestration in Rust — Round 0"," ","-**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs`","+**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs`, modify `batch_sumcheck_uni_round0_poly`"," ","-In `batch_sumcheck_uni_round0_poly`:","-1. Group `trace_ptrs` by (trace_height, sign_of_n) — traces that would accumulate into the same G buffer with the same kernel configuration.","-2. For each group: build descriptor array on host, upload to device, launch batched kernel.","-3. Use existing final_reduce pattern to accumulate block sums into G buffers.","+Replace the per-trace loop (lines 504-549) with:"," ","-In `fold_ple_evals`:","-1. Group traces by trace_height.","-2. For each group: build descriptor array, upload, launch batched kernel.","+1. **Pre-sort by height** (already sorted via `ht_diff_idxs`): Iterate `trace_ptrs` and group consecutive traces with the same `trace_height` into batches."," ","-**Threshold**: Only use batched path when group has ≥ 10 traces. Below that, the descriptor overhead exceeds the launch savings.","+2. **Pre-compute max block_sums size**: `max_block_sums_len = max over all traces of _stacked_reduction_r0_required_temp_buffer_size(h, w, l_skip)`. Allocate `self.d_block_sums` once at this size."," ","-### Change 5: Pre-allocate block_sums buffer","+3. **For each height group** (traces with same `trace_height`):","+   a. If group has < 10 traces: process sequentially (existing code path)","+   b. If group has ≥ 10 traces:","+      - Build `Vec<StackedR0Desc>` on host. Each descriptor's `lambda_pows` field = `self.d_lambda_pows.as_ptr() + 2 * window_start_for_this_trace`. The `window_start_for_this_trace` is computed from the corresponding `ht_diff_idxs[i]`.","+      - Upload descriptor array to device: `descs.to_device()`","+      - Compute total blocks needed: sum of `blocks_for_this_desc` across all descriptors in group","+      - Allocate shared block_sums buffer for all descriptors: `total_blocks * NUM_G * skip_domain`","+      - Launch batched `block_sum` kernel with `grid = total_blocks`","+      - For each descriptor in the group: call `final_reduce_block_sums<true>` to accumulate that descriptor's block sums into the appropriate `d_g_output` buffer","+   ","+   Note: All traces of the same height have the same `n`, so they all accumulate into the same G bucket (`d_g_pos` or `d_g_neg[k]`)."," ","-Currently, `self.d_block_sums` is resized per trace (line 529-531). With batched launches, pre-allocate a block_sums buffer large enough for the largest batch at the start of round 0.","+### Change 5: Orchestration in Rust — PLE fold"," ","+**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs`, modify `fold_ple_evals`","+","+Batching is scoped **within** the per-commit outer loop (lines 703-745). Within each commit:","+","+1. Group traces by `trace.height()`.","+2. For groups with ≥ 10 traces: build `FoldPleDesc` array, upload, launch batched kernel. Each descriptor's `dst` = `folded_evals.as_mut_ptr() + dst_offset_for_this_trace` (pre-computed from the sequential scan).","+3. For groups with < 10 traces: use existing per-trace path.","+","+The per-commit `q_evals.push(folded_evals)` logic is unchanged.","+"," ## Invariants"," ","-1. **Correctness**: Each trace in the batch produces the same G0/G1/G2 partial sums as the per-trace path. The final reduction accumulates them identically. The bitwise output is identical to the sequential path (modulo floating point associativity, which doesn't apply to finite field arithmetic).","+1. **Correctness**: Each trace produces the same G0/G1/G2 partial block sums via the same kernel body. The block sums are reduced and added to G output identically. The fold_ple writes to the same per-trace non-overlapping output regions. Output is bit-identical to the sequential path."," ","-2. **APC 0 no-regression**: At APC 0, there are ~20 traces per segment. Most groups will have < 10 traces, falling below the batching threshold. The sequential path runs unchanged.","+2. **APC 0 no-regression**: At APC 0, ~20 traces per segment. Most height groups have < 10 traces, falling below the batching threshold. The sequential path runs unchanged."," ","-3. **Output buffer safety**: The round 0 batched kernel writes to block_sums (not directly to G output). The final reduce kernel adds block_sums into G output. This matches the current per-trace pattern where block_sums is a temporary buffer.","+3. **No VPMM pool impact**: Descriptor arrays are tiny (~400 × 24 bytes = ~10 KB). The block_sums pre-allocation replaces per-trace resizing with one upfront allocation. No per-thread accumulation buffers (the failure mode of `multistream-stacked-reduction-round0` which allocated 112 DeviceBuffers). Net memory impact is negligible."," ","-4. **No VPMM pool impact**: The descriptor arrays are small (400 descriptors × 24 bytes = ~10 KB). The block_sums pre-allocation replaces per-trace resizing with a single upfront allocation. Net memory impact is negligible.","+4. **fold_ple per-commit boundary**: Batching is scoped within each commit's trace loop. The per-commit `folded_evals` allocation and `q_evals.push` are unchanged."," ","-5. **fold_ple output correctness**: Each trace's folded output is written to a non-overlapping region of the q_evals buffer (indexed by dst_offset). The batched kernel uses per-descriptor dst pointers that match the sequential per-trace offsets exactly.","+5. **lambda_pows offsets**: Each descriptor's `lambda_pows` is set to `d_lambda_pows.as_ptr() + 2 * ht_diff_idxs[i]` where `i` is the trace's index in `trace_ptrs`. This matches the current sequential computation at line 535."," "," ## Measurement Plan"," ","-1. Run benchmark for APC 0, 100, 300 before and after the change.","+1. Run benchmark for APC 0, 100, 300 before and after."," 2. Compare `prover.openings.stacked_reduction.round0_time_ms` per segment.","-3. Compare `STARK (excl. trace)` overall.","+3. Compare `STARK (excl. trace)` overall via `spec.py`."," 4. Run nsight profile on APC 300 to verify:","-   - `stacked_reduction_round0_block_sum_kernel` instance count decreased (from ~797 to ~80-100)","+   - `stacked_reduction_round0_block_sum_kernel` instance count decreased (797 → ~80-120)","+   - `stacked_reduction_fold_ple_kernel` instance count decreased similarly","+   - `final_reduce_block_sums<true>` instance count unchanged (~797)","    - Total kernel GPU time unchanged or slightly improved","-   - No new kernel time regression in other phases","-5. APC 0 must show no regression (within ±10ms noise).","+5. APC 0 must show no regression (within ±10ms noise on STARK excl trace)."," "," ### Expected results"," ","-- Stacked Reduction Round 0 per segment: 14ms → 10-12ms (seg0), 12ms → 9-11ms (seg1)","-- STARK excl trace APC 300: 1101ms → ~1087-1093ms (8-14ms improvement)","+- Launch overhead reduction: ~1400 eliminated launches × ~5µs = ~7ms across full benchmark","+- Per-segment stacked reduction round 0: 14ms → 10-12ms (seg0), 12ms → 9-11ms (seg1)","+- STARK excl trace APC 300: 1101ms → ~1087-1095ms (~6-14ms improvement)"," - APC 0: no change (below batching threshold)"," "," ## Rollback Criteria"]}],"originalFile":"# Plan: Batch Stacked Reduction Round 0 Descriptor Arrays\n\n## Goal\n\nReduce kernel launch overhead in the stacked reduction Round 0 by batching per-trace kernel launches into per-height-group batched launches using descriptor arrays. At APC 300, the stacked reduction Round 0 calls `stacked_reduction_sumcheck_round0` and `stacked_reduction_fold_ple` once per backing trace matrix (~400 per segment across all commits), with many being tiny (1-2 columns, height 2^5-2^8). By grouping same-height traces into single batched kernel launches, we reduce ~800 kernel launches per segment to ~80, saving ~720 launches × ~5µs = ~3.6ms per segment.\n\n## Current Code Path\n\n### Round 0 sumcheck loop\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs`, lines 504-549\n\n```rust\nfor ((trace_ptr, trace_height, trace_width), window) in zip(\n    mem::take(&mut self.trace_ptrs),\n    self.ht_diff_idxs.windows(2),\n) {\n    let n = log_height as isize - l_skip as isize;\n    let d_g_output = if n >= 0 { &mut d_g_pos } else { &mut d_g_neg[(-n-1) as usize] };\n\n    // Per-trace temp buffer\n    if block_sums_len > self.d_block_sums.len() {\n        self.d_block_sums = DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(block_sums_len);\n    }\n\n    stacked_reduction_sumcheck_round0(\n        &self.eq_r_ns, trace_ptr, lambda_pows_ptr,\n        &mut self.d_block_sums, d_g_output,\n        trace_height, trace_width, l_skip,\n    );\n}\n```\n\nEach call launches a CUDA kernel that computes G0, G1, G2 partial sums for one trace matrix, then a final reduction kernel that ADDs block sums into the output bucket.\n\n### PLE fold loop\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs`, lines 714-743\n\n```rust\nfor trace in &stacked.traces {\n    stacked_reduction_fold_ple(\n        trace.buffer().as_ptr(), dst,\n        &self.d_omega_skip_pows, &d_inv_lagrange_denoms,\n        trace.height(), trace.width(), l_skip,\n    );\n    dst_offset += new_height * trace.width();\n}\n```\n\nEach call launches one CUDA kernel that folds a single trace's PLE evaluations.\n\n### CUDA kernel signatures\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/stacked_reduction.rs`, lines 44-63\n\n```c\n// Round 0: computes G0, G1, G2 block sums + final reduction\n_stacked_reduction_sumcheck_round0(\n    eq_r_ns, trace_ptr, lambda_pows, block_sums, output,\n    trace_height, trace_width, l_skip, num_x);\n\n// PLE fold: folds trace evals by Lagrange interpolation at u_0\n_stacked_reduction_fold_ple(\n    src, dst, omega_skip_pows, inv_lagrange_denoms,\n    trace_height, trace_width, l_skip);\n```\n\n### nsight kernel data (APC 300)\n\n- `stacked_reduction_round0_block_sum_kernel`: 22ms total, 797 instances, avg 28µs\n- `stacked_reduction_fold_ple_kernel`: 9ms total, 797 instances, avg 11µs\n- Total: 31ms GPU, ~26ms wall clock (37ms + 36ms for 2 segments minus MLE portion)\n- Per-segment round 0 wall clock: 14ms (seg0), 12ms (seg1) = 26ms total\n- The ~400 launches per segment include traces from common_main + preprocessed + cached_main commits\n\n## Changes\n\n### Change 1: Add batched Round 0 CUDA kernel\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/sumcheck.cu` (or a new file `stacked_reduction_batched.cu`)\n\nAdd a descriptor struct and batched kernel:\n\n```c\nstruct StackedR0Desc {\n    const Fp *trace_ptr;\n    const FpExt *lambda_pows;  // already offset to this trace's position\n    uint32_t trace_width;\n};\n\n// Batched kernel: processes all traces of the same height in one launch.\n// Each block processes one trace in the descriptor array.\n// Uses atomicAdd to accumulate into shared G output buffer.\n__global__ void batched_stacked_reduction_round0_kernel(\n    const FpExt *eq_r_ns,\n    const StackedR0Desc *descs,\n    const uint32_t *block_starts,  // prefix sum: which desc this block belongs to\n    uint32_t num_descs,\n    FpExt *block_sums,    // [total_blocks * NUM_G * skip_domain]\n    uint32_t trace_height, // same for all in this batch\n    uint32_t l_skip\n);\n```\n\nThe existing per-trace kernel body can be reused: each block computes partial G sums for its assigned trace, writing to its segment of block_sums. A final reduction kernel sums all block_sums into the G output.\n\n**Key design**: Use the `BlockCtx` binary-search pattern from the batch MLE kernel (`crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/batch_mle.cu`) to map blocks to descriptors.\n\n### Change 2: Add batched PLE fold CUDA kernel\n\nSame approach: descriptor array with per-trace src/dst pointers.\n\n```c\nstruct FoldPleDesc {\n    const Fp *src;        // trace buffer\n    FpExt *dst;           // output buffer (already offset)\n    uint32_t trace_width;\n};\n\n__global__ void batched_stacked_reduction_fold_ple_kernel(\n    const FoldPleDesc *descs,\n    const uint32_t *block_starts,\n    uint32_t num_descs,\n    const Fp *omega_skip_pows,\n    const FpExt *inv_lagrange_denoms,\n    uint32_t trace_height,\n    uint32_t l_skip\n);\n```\n\n### Change 3: Add FFI bindings\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/stacked_reduction.rs`\n\nAdd `repr(C)` structs for `StackedR0Desc` and `FoldPleDesc`, plus extern \"C\" declarations and safe wrapper functions.\n\n### Change 4: Orchestration in Rust\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs`\n\nIn `batch_sumcheck_uni_round0_poly`:\n1. Group `trace_ptrs` by (trace_height, sign_of_n) — traces that would accumulate into the same G buffer with the same kernel configuration.\n2. For each group: build descriptor array on host, upload to device, launch batched kernel.\n3. Use existing final_reduce pattern to accumulate block sums into G buffers.\n\nIn `fold_ple_evals`:\n1. Group traces by trace_height.\n2. For each group: build descriptor array, upload, launch batched kernel.\n\n**Threshold**: Only use batched path when group has ≥ 10 traces. Below that, the descriptor overhead exceeds the launch savings.\n\n### Change 5: Pre-allocate block_sums buffer\n\nCurrently, `self.d_block_sums` is resized per trace (line 529-531). With batched launches, pre-allocate a block_sums buffer large enough for the largest batch at the start of round 0.\n\n## Invariants\n\n1. **Correctness**: Each trace in the batch produces the same G0/G1/G2 partial sums as the per-trace path. The final reduction accumulates them identically. The bitwise output is identical to the sequential path (modulo floating point associativity, which doesn't apply to finite field arithmetic).\n\n2. **APC 0 no-regression**: At APC 0, there are ~20 traces per segment. Most groups will have < 10 traces, falling below the batching threshold. The sequential path runs unchanged.\n\n3. **Output buffer safety**: The round 0 batched kernel writes to block_sums (not directly to G output). The final reduce kernel adds block_sums into G output. This matches the current per-trace pattern where block_sums is a temporary buffer.\n\n4. **No VPMM pool impact**: The descriptor arrays are small (400 descriptors × 24 bytes = ~10 KB). The block_sums pre-allocation replaces per-trace resizing with a single upfront allocation. Net memory impact is negligible.\n\n5. **fold_ple output correctness**: Each trace's folded output is written to a non-overlapping region of the q_evals buffer (indexed by dst_offset). The batched kernel uses per-descriptor dst pointers that match the sequential per-trace offsets exactly.\n\n## Measurement Plan\n\n1. Run benchmark for APC 0, 100, 300 before and after the change.\n2. Compare `prover.openings.stacked_reduction.round0_time_ms` per segment.\n3. Compare `STARK (excl. trace)` overall.\n4. Run nsight profile on APC 300 to verify:\n   - `stacked_reduction_round0_block_sum_kernel` instance count decreased (from ~797 to ~80-100)\n   - Total kernel GPU time unchanged or slightly improved\n   - No new kernel time regression in other phases\n5. APC 0 must show no regression (within ±10ms noise).\n\n### Expected results\n\n- Stacked Reduction Round 0 per segment: 14ms → 10-12ms (seg0), 12ms → 9-11ms (seg1)\n- STARK excl trace APC 300: 1101ms → ~1087-1093ms (8-14ms improvement)\n- APC 0: no change (below batching threshold)\n\n## Rollback Criteria\n\n- Less than 5ms improvement on stacked reduction round 0 total at APC 300.\n- Any regression > 10ms on STARK excl trace at APC 0.\n- Any correctness failure (proof verification fails at any APC configuration).\n"}}
