{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BwVrXmKDWmmourSSqw8MJ9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Plan: Batch Stacked Reduction Round 0 Descriptor Arrays\n2\t\n3\t*Note: Directory name is a misnomer from the first plan iteration. The actual optimization targets stacked reduction Round 0 batching, matching task.md.*\n4\t\n5\t## Goal\n6\t\n7\tReduce kernel launch overhead in the stacked reduction Round 0 by batching per-trace kernel launches into per-height-group batched launches using descriptor arrays. At APC 300, the stacked reduction Round 0 calls `_stacked_reduction_sumcheck_round0` (which launches 2 CUDA kernels: `stacked_reduction_round0_block_sum_kernel` + `final_reduce_block_sums<true>`) and `_stacked_reduction_fold_ple` (1 kernel) once per backing trace matrix (~400 per segment). The current total is 2391 kernel launches across both segments (797 × 3 kernel types). By batching same-height traces, we eliminate ~1400 launches.\n8\t\n9\t## Current Code Path\n10\t\n11\t### Round 0 sumcheck loop\n12\t\n13\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs`, lines 504-549\n14\t\n15\t```rust\n16\tfor ((trace_ptr, trace_height, trace_width), window) in zip(\n17\t    mem::take(&mut self.trace_ptrs),\n18\t    self.ht_diff_idxs.windows(2),\n19\t) {\n20\t    let log_height = trace_height.ilog2();\n21\t    let n = log_height as isize - l_skip as isize;\n22\t    let d_g_output = if n >= 0 { &mut d_g_pos } else { &mut d_g_neg[(-n-1) as usize] };\n23\t\n24\t    let block_sums_len = _stacked_reduction_r0_required_temp_buffer_size(\n25\t        trace_height as u32, trace_width as u32, l_skip as u32) as usize;\n26\t    if block_sums_len > self.d_block_sums.len() {\n27\t        self.d_block_sums = DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(block_sums_len);\n28\t    }\n29\t\n30\t    let lambda_pows_ptr = self.d_lambda_pows.as_ptr().add(2 * window[0]);\n31\t    stacked_reduction_sumcheck_round0(\n32\t        &self.eq_r_ns, trace_ptr, lambda_pows_ptr,\n33\t        &mut self.d_block_sums, d_g_output,\n34\t        trace_height, trace_width, l_skip,\n35\t    );\n36\t}\n37\t```\n38\t\n39\tEach `stacked_reduction_sumcheck_round0` call launches TWO CUDA kernels:\n40\t1. `stacked_reduction_round0_block_sum_kernel` — computes G0, G1, G2 partial block sums\n41\t2. `final_reduce_block_sums<true>` — reduces block sums and ADDs into the G output buffer\n42\t\n43\t### PLE fold loop\n44\t\n45\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs`, lines 703-745\n46\t\n47\t```rust\n48\tfor stacked in &self.stacked_per_commit {                // <-- per-commit loop\n49\t    let folded_evals = DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(...);\n50\t    folded_evals.fill_zero()?;\n51\t    let mut dst_offset = 0;\n52\t    for trace in &stacked.traces {                        // <-- per-trace loop\n53\t        stacked_reduction_fold_ple(\n54\t            trace.buffer().as_ptr(),\n55\t            folded_evals.as_mut_ptr().add(dst_offset),\n56\t            &self.d_omega_skip_pows, &d_inv_lagrange_denoms,\n57\t            trace.height(), trace.width(), l_skip,\n58\t        );\n59\t        dst_offset += new_height * trace.width();\n60\t    }\n61\t    self.q_evals.push(folded_evals);                      // per-commit output\n62\t}\n63\t```\n64\t\n65\tThe fold_ple loop is nested: outer loop per commit (each commit has its own `folded_evals` buffer), inner loop per trace within that commit.\n66\t\n67\t### CUDA kernel signatures\n68\t\n69\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/stacked_reduction.rs`, lines 44-63\n70\t\n71\t```c\n72\tfn _stacked_reduction_sumcheck_round0(\n73\t    eq_r_ns, trace_ptr, lambda_pows, block_sums, output,\n74\t    trace_height, trace_width, l_skip, num_x) -> i32;\n75\t\n76\tfn _stacked_reduction_fold_ple(\n77\t    src, dst, omega_skip_pows, inv_lagrange_denoms,\n78\t    trace_height, trace_width, l_skip) -> i32;\n79\t```\n80\t\n81\t### nsight kernel data (APC 300, full benchmark including recursion)\n82\t\n83\t- `stacked_reduction_round0_block_sum_kernel`: 22ms total, 797 instances, avg 28µs\n84\t- `final_reduce_block_sums<true>`: 7.8ms total, 797 instances, avg 10µs\n85\t- `stacked_reduction_fold_ple_kernel`: 9ms total, 797 instances, avg 11µs\n86\t- **Total: 38.8ms GPU, 2391 kernel launches**\n87\t\n88\tPer-segment wall clock:\n89\t- Stacked reduction round 0: 14ms (seg0) + 12ms (seg1) = 26ms total\n90\t- Of this, the GPU kernel time is ~15ms per segment (from 38.8ms / ~2.5 segments+recursion)\n91\t- The remaining ~11ms per segment is kernel launch overhead, block_sums resize, lambda_pows pointer arithmetic\n92\t\n93\t### Grouping analysis\n94\t\n95\tTraces within a segment are grouped by height (same `n = log_height - l_skip`). At APC 300:\n96\t- ~20 distinct heights per segment\n97\t- Some heights have 200+ traces (e.g., APC traces with height 2^4)\n98\t- Others have 1-5 traces (large AIRs with height 2^18+)\n99\t\n100\tSince `n = log_height - l_skip`, all traces of the same height map to the same G output bucket. Grouping by `trace_height` is sufficient.\n101\t\n102\t## Changes\n103\t\n104\t### Change 1: Add batched Round 0 block_sum CUDA kernel\n105\t\n106\t**File**: New file `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/stacked_reduction_batched.cu`\n107\t\n108\t```c\n109\tstruct StackedR0Desc {\n110\t    const Fp *trace_ptr;\n111\t    const FpExt *lambda_pows;  // pre-offset: self.d_lambda_pows.as_ptr() + 2 * window[0]\n112\t    uint32_t trace_width;\n113\t    uint32_t blocks_for_this_desc;  // number of grid blocks assigned to this descriptor\n114\t};\n115\t\n116\t// Maps a global blockIdx.x to a (descriptor_index, local_block_index) pair\n117\t// using binary search on the prefix-sum of blocks_for_this_desc.\n118\t// Follows the BlockCtx pattern from batch_mle.cu.\n119\t```\n120\t\n121\tThe batched kernel reuses the existing per-trace kernel body. Each block is assigned to one descriptor via the `BlockCtx` binary search. Block sums are written to `block_sums[global_block_offset * NUM_G * skip_domain]`.\n122\t\n123\t**Final reduce strategy**: Call `final_reduce_block_sums<true>` per-descriptor after the batched block_sum kernel. This keeps the final reduce unchanged and simple. With ~20 height groups per segment and 1 final_reduce per descriptor within each group, the total final_reduce calls stay at ~400 per segment — but each reduce processes the blocks from just one descriptor. This is identical to the current behavior for each descriptor.\n124\t\n125\tRationale: The final_reduce kernel is tiny (10µs avg, 7.8ms total). Keeping it per-descriptor avoids implementing a batched reduce, adds zero risk, and the 400 launches × 5µs = 2ms overhead is acceptable relative to the savings from batching the larger block_sum kernel.\n126\t\n127\t### Change 2: Add batched PLE fold CUDA kernel\n128\t\n129\t**File**: Same file `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/stacked_reduction_batched.cu`\n130\t\n131\t```c\n132\tstruct FoldPleDesc {\n133\t    const Fp *src;        // trace buffer pointer\n134\t    FpExt *dst;           // output buffer pointer (pre-offset within per-commit folded_evals)\n135\t    uint32_t trace_width;\n136\t};\n137\t```\n138\t\n139\tSame BlockCtx binary search pattern. Each block processes elements from one descriptor.\n140\t\n141\t### Change 3: Add FFI bindings\n142\t\n143\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/stacked_reduction.rs`\n144\t\n145\tAdd `repr(C)` structs for `StackedR0Desc` and `FoldPleDesc`, extern \"C\" declarations for the batched launchers, and safe Rust wrapper functions.\n146\t\n147\t### Change 4: Orchestration in Rust — Round 0\n148\t\n149\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs`, modify `batch_sumcheck_uni_round0_poly`\n150\t\n151\tReplace the per-trace loop (lines 504-549) with:\n152\t\n153\t1. **Pre-sort by height** (already sorted via `ht_diff_idxs`): Iterate `trace_ptrs` and group consecutive traces with the same `trace_height` into batches.\n154\t\n155\t2. **Pre-compute max block_sums size**: `max_block_sums_len = max over all traces of _stacked_reduction_r0_required_temp_buffer_size(h, w, l_skip)`. Allocate `self.d_block_sums` once at this size.\n156\t\n157\t3. **For each height group** (traces with same `trace_height`):\n158\t   a. If group has < 10 traces: process sequentially (existing code path)\n159\t   b. If group has ≥ 10 traces:\n160\t      - Build `Vec<StackedR0Desc>` on host. Each descriptor's `lambda_pows` field = `self.d_lambda_pows.as_ptr() + 2 * window_start_for_this_trace`. The `window_start_for_this_trace` is computed from the corresponding `ht_diff_idxs[i]`.\n161\t      - Upload descriptor array to device: `descs.to_device()`\n162\t      - Compute total blocks needed: sum of `blocks_for_this_desc` across all descriptors in group\n163\t      - Allocate shared block_sums buffer for all descriptors: `total_blocks * NUM_G * skip_domain`\n164\t      - Launch batched `block_sum` kernel with `grid = total_blocks`\n165\t      - For each descriptor in the group: call `final_reduce_block_sums<true>` to accumulate that descriptor's block sums into the appropriate `d_g_output` buffer\n166\t   \n167\t   Note: All traces of the same height have the same `n`, so they all accumulate into the same G bucket (`d_g_pos` or `d_g_neg[k]`).\n168\t\n169\t### Change 5: Orchestration in Rust — PLE fold\n170\t\n171\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs`, modify `fold_ple_evals`\n172\t\n173\tBatching is scoped **within** the per-commit outer loop (lines 703-745). Within each commit:\n174\t\n175\t1. Group traces by `trace.height()`.\n176\t2. For groups with ≥ 10 traces: build `FoldPleDesc` array, upload, launch batched kernel. Each descriptor's `dst` = `folded_evals.as_mut_ptr() + dst_offset_for_this_trace` (pre-computed from the sequential scan).\n177\t3. For groups with < 10 traces: use existing per-trace path.\n178\t\n179\tThe per-commit `q_evals.push(folded_evals)` logic is unchanged.\n180\t\n181\t## Invariants\n182\t\n183\t1. **Correctness**: Each trace produces the same G0/G1/G2 partial block sums via the same kernel body. The block sums are reduced and added to G output identically. The fold_ple writes to the same per-trace non-overlapping output regions. Output is bit-identical to the sequential path.\n184\t\n185\t2. **APC 0 no-regression**: At APC 0, ~20 traces per segment. Most height groups have < 10 traces, falling below the batching threshold. The sequential path runs unchanged.\n186\t\n187\t3. **No VPMM pool impact**: Descriptor arrays are tiny (~400 × 24 bytes = ~10 KB). The block_sums pre-allocation replaces per-trace resizing with one upfront allocation. No per-thread accumulation buffers (the failure mode of `multistream-stacked-reduction-round0` which allocated 112 DeviceBuffers). Net memory impact is negligible.\n188\t\n189\t4. **fold_ple per-commit boundary**: Batching is scoped within each commit's trace loop. The per-commit `folded_evals` allocation and `q_evals.push` are unchanged.\n190\t\n191\t5. **lambda_pows offsets**: Each descriptor's `lambda_pows` is set to `d_lambda_pows.as_ptr() + 2 * ht_diff_idxs[i]` where `i` is the trace's index in `trace_ptrs`. This matches the current sequential computation at line 535.\n192\t\n193\t## Measurement Plan\n194\t\n195\t1. Run benchmark for APC 0, 100, 300 before and after.\n196\t2. Compare `prover.openings.stacked_reduction.round0_time_ms` per segment.\n197\t3. Compare `STARK (excl. trace)` overall via `spec.py`.\n198\t4. Run nsight profile on APC 300 to verify:\n199\t   - `stacked_reduction_round0_block_sum_kernel` instance count decreased (797 → ~80-120)\n200\t   - `stacked_reduction_fold_ple_kernel` instance count decreased similarly\n201\t   - `final_reduce_block_sums<true>` instance count unchanged (~797)\n202\t   - Total kernel GPU time unchanged or slightly improved\n203\t5. APC 0 must show no regression (within ±10ms noise on STARK excl trace).\n204\t\n205\t### Expected results\n206\t\n207\t- Launch overhead reduction: ~1400 eliminated launches × ~5µs = ~7ms across full benchmark\n208\t- Per-segment stacked reduction round 0: 14ms → 10-12ms (seg0), 12ms → 9-11ms (seg1)\n209\t- STARK excl trace APC 300: 1101ms → ~1087-1095ms (~6-14ms improvement)\n210\t- APC 0: no change (below batching threshold)\n211\t\n212\t## Rollback Criteria\n213\t\n214\t- Less than 5ms improvement on stacked reduction round 0 total at APC 300.\n215\t- Any regression > 10ms on STARK excl trace at APC 0.\n216\t- Any correctness failure (proof verification fails at any APC configuration).\n217\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01U1pThytWdwaKib3x42wLgC","session_id":"97849a12-7ea3-4743-9ec4-4f09ecc25100","uuid":"cadfa129-5bfc-42e9-afcd-a92794391b4f","timestamp":"2026-04-16T14:32:44.398Z"}
